WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.135
Your team rents a giant AI model by the token

2
00:00:03.135 --> 00:00:05.710
to do the same small job, over and over.

3
00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:07.670
Your CFO wants the bill down.

4
00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:10.400
Your engineers want proof it won't break.

5
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.634
FallForge Mint starts with the question nobody asks:

6
00:00:13.634 --> 00:00:14.961
which model is enough?

7
00:00:14.961 --> 00:00:19.059
The sizer picks the smallest open-weight model that clears your bar.

8
00:00:19.059 --> 00:00:21.450
A one-billion answer says one billion.

9
00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:23.966
Mint it from a few of your own examples.

10
00:00:23.966 --> 00:00:27.831
Then it tries to beat the base model on examples it's never seen

11
00:00:27.831 --> 00:00:29.380
and it can say you lost.

12
00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:31.080
You get a signed scorecard.

13
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:34.576
The held-out answers weren't in the spec we gave the model.

14
00:00:34.576 --> 00:00:35.920
Anyone can re-run it.

15
00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:39.977
At high use, owning can run six to seventeen times cheaper.

16
00:00:39.977 --> 00:00:42.760
When renting wins, it says keep renting.

17
00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:43.641
One file.

18
00:00:43.641 --> 00:00:44.769
Your machine.

19
00:00:44.769 --> 00:00:45.650
No meter.

20
00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:49.252
And Forge is one door into a whole sovereign estate.

21
00:00:49.252 --> 00:00:51.170
Seven stages, one pipeline.

22
00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:53.177
Everything rides a trust rail

23
00:00:53.177 --> 00:00:55.676
a gate that tries to break every test.

24
00:00:55.676 --> 00:00:59.590
It even found a line left-pad's passing tests don't check.

25
00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:03.574
In fall-os, you hatch your own assistant and level it into your own

26
00:01:03.574 --> 00:01:04.660
operating system.

27
00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:06.727
The dispatcher routes every job:

28
00:01:06.727 --> 00:01:10.968
seven organs run themselves, nine wait for a human key, and eight are

29
00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:12.420
honestly marked to-do.

30
00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:15.334
Peers connect directly, no server between

31
00:01:15.334 --> 00:01:18.110
and sovereign-foundry ties it together.

32
00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:21.303
Models trained on their own output lose the tails.

33
00:01:21.303 --> 00:01:23.902
A mesh of real people is the clean signal.

34
00:01:23.902 --> 00:01:25.920
Owned, provable AI is the moat.

35
00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:27.809
AI Native Solutions.

36
00:01:27.809 --> 00:01:28.435
Own it.

37
00:01:28.435 --> 00:01:29.590
Prove it.

